[11693]="70047E27\n1\tComplete to receive a map to the Party Tree!\tIn celebration of another year in Middle-earth, the hobbits from the Shire have left fun lists of things to do hanging from the Party Tree.\n2\tComplete to receive a map to the Party Tree!\tIn celebration of another year in Middle-earth, the hobbits from the Shire have left fun lists of things to do hanging from the Party Tree.\n",
[11694]="70066004\n1\tToss a coin to the first harper\030Toss a coin to the second harper\030Toss a coin to the third harper\030Toss a coin to the fourth harper\030Toss a coin to the fifth harper\tLothíriel has asked you to listen to songs about the Rohirrim, and report back with what you hear. You should toss a coin to the minstrels in Harper's Court. Harper's Court is in Dol Amroth.\n2\tReturn to Lothíriel\tYou listened to many tales and ballads of Éomer for the lady, Lothíriel. You should return to her in the Court of the Prince, in Dol Amroth.\n",
[11695]="7004E7EA\n1\tSurvive the Expedition into the Anvil\tKarazgar has come to the Anvil of Winterstith to bolster his forces by laying claim to the Herald of Winter and her Frost-horde. If he succeeds, he will have the means to wipe out not only the expedition of dwarves in Ered Mithrin, but to lay siege to all of the Northern Kingdoms.\n2\tTalk to Hórin\tHórin is standing by outside the Anvil. You should talk to Hórin.\n",
[11696]="70050227\n1\tReport to Hórin in Skarháld\tHórin wishes to speak with you. He can be found within Skarháld.\n2\tReport to Hórin in Skarháld\tHórin wishes to speak with you. He can be found within Skarháld.\n3\tTalk to Hórin at the Wyrmgap\tHórin has gone to the Wyrmgap to meet his scout. You should head to the Wyrmgap and speak to Hórin.\n4\tTalk to Nori\tNori would like you speak with you. You should talk to Nori.\n5\tTalk to Náth\tNáth would like to speak with you. You should talk to Náth.\n6\tTalk to Hórin\tThe Stout-axes would like to join the company traveling into the Withered Heath. You should talk to Hórin.\n7\tDiscover the entrance to the Anvil of Winterstith\tThe dwarves are going ahead to find a way to the Anvil of Winterstith. You should discover the entrance to the Anvil of Winterstith in the Withered Heath.\n8\tClaim a bone from the corpse of Vethúg Wintermind\030Complete the Anvil of Winterstith\tEnter the Anvil of Winterstith through the Instance Finder panel. Claim a bone from the corpse of Vethúg Wintermind, and survive your expedition into the Anvil.\n9\tTalk to Hórin\tHórin is standing by outside the Anvil, East of here. You should talk to Hórin.\n10\tTalk to Nori at the Wyrmgap\tNori can be found at the Wyrmgap, waiting to hear news of your expedition. You should return to Nori now that you have slain Vethúg Wintermind.\n",
[11697]="70051879\n1\tDefeat Isvítha the Gluttonous\tIsvítha the Gluttonous, a massive frost worm, guards the entrance to the Anvil of Winterstith. You must defeat her to gain entrance.\n2\tDefeat the Thirteen Kings\tDragon-spell spectres of the Zhélruka kings who died seeking the fabled Thafar-gathol haunt the Anvil of Winterstith, blocking your passage.\n3\tDefeat Karazgar the Weeping Warrior\tKarazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has ventured into the Anvil to claim the Herald of Winter and her Frost-horde. You must find and defeat him before that can happen.\n4\tSurvive your encounter with Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, is one of the most powerful and ancient creatures in Middle-earth, and you have just stumbled into her lair.\n5\tCompleted: The Anvil of Winterstith (Tier 1)\tYou have completed the Anvil of Winterstith on Tier 1\n",
[11698]="70051878\n1\tDefeat Isvítha the Gluttonous\tIsvítha the Gluttonous, a massive frost worm, guards the entrance to the Anvil of Winterstith. You must defeat her to gain entrance.\n2\tDefeat the Thirteen Kings\tDragon-spell spectres of the Zhélruka kings who died seeking the fabled Thafar-gathol haunt the Anvil of Winterstith, blocking your passage.\n3\tDefeat Karazgar the Weeping Warrior\tKarazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has ventured into the Anvil to claim the Herald of Winter and her Frost-horde. You must find and defeat him before that can happen.\n4\tSurvive your encounter with Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, is one of the most powerful and ancient creatures in Middle-earth, and you have just stumbled into her lair.\n5\tCompleted: The Anvil of Winterstith (Tier 2)\tYou have completed the Anvil of Winterstith on Tier 2\n",
[11699]="70051877\n1\tDefeat Isvítha the Gluttonous\tIsvítha the Gluttonous, a massive frost worm, guards the entrance to the Anvil of Winterstith. You must defeat her to gain entry.\n2\tDefeat the Thirteen Kings\tDragon-spell spectres of the Zhélruka kings who died seeking the fabled Thafar-gathol haunt the Anvil of Winterstith, blocking your passage.\n3\tDefeat Karazgar the Weeping Warrior\tKarazgar, the Weeping Warrior, has ventured into the Anvil to claim the Herald of Winter and her Frost-horde. You must find and defeat him before that can happen.\n4\tSurvive your encounter with Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, is one of the most powerful and ancient creatures in Middle-earth, and you have just stumbled into her lair.\n5\tCompleted: The Anvil of Winterstith (Tier 3)\tYou have completed the Anvil of Winterstith on Tier 3\n",
[11700]="7005AF6B\n1\tComplete 'Instance: The Apprentices Attack'\tIt is time for you to carry out Ausma's plan.\n2\tTalk to Krystig\tTroubling portents abound! Where is Ausma?\n3\tFind a clue to Ausma's whereabouts\tTroubling portents abound! Where is Ausma?\n4\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig awaits your unhappy tidings.\n",
[11701]="700529D1\n1\tComplete: 'Instance: Dawn's Arrival'\tBaradal is now free, but she is injured from the warg attack. You should talk to Baradal to begin Instance: Dawn's Arrival.\n2\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal has been taken to the Galadhrim camp on the border of Lothlórien. You should talk to Baradal.\n",
[11702]="70062DD6\n1\tFind the bridge to the north of Caras Gelebren\030Find the river-bank to the south-west of Echad Terthas\030Find the slope to the south-east of Echad Terthas\tIlarion asked you to scout several approaches to Caras Gelebren: the bridge to the north, the river-bank to the south-west, and the sloping hill to the south-east.\n2\tTalk to Ilarion at Echad Terthas\tIlarion is at Echad Terthas, waiting for your report.\n",
[11703]="7000256B\n1\tDefeat gertheryg in Maethad (total: 8)\030Defeat trolls in Maethad (total: 8)\tThe arena of Maethad is north and east of Gabilshathûr. Hwati has asked you to find the arena and thin the numbers of gertheryg and trolls training within.\n2\tTalk to Hwati\tHwati is back at Gabilshathûr, west and south of Maethad. Having defeated a number of gertheryg and trolls, you should return to Hwati.\n",
[11704]="7002EE01\n1\tCraft spears for the guards of Eaworth\tThe blacksmith's forge is in Eaworth, near the Mead Hall. Goldwine asked you to forge spears for the guards of Eaworth.\n2\tThe guards of Eaworth can be found throughout the city. Goldwine asked you to bring the spears you crafted to the guards of Eaworth.\t\n3\tTalk to Goldwine\tGoldwine stands guard near the blacksmith's forge in Eaworth. You should let Goldwine know that you have delivered the spears to the guards of Eaworth.\n",
